# therapyportal-mcp reads one TherapyNotes client portal
# (https://www.therapyportal.com/p/<practice>/). It lists appointments,
# documents, forms, balances, receipts and secure messages, and downloads
# completed documents and receipts. NOT read-only: it also sends secure messages
# and uploads files in answer to document requests, each confirm-gated. It signs
# and pays nothing.

# The practice code — the part after /p/ in your portal URL. Required.
# THERAPYPORTAL_PRACTICE=

# Server-side password login (the default transport when both are set). A
# rejected sign-in is never retried automatically.
# THERAPYPORTAL_EMAIL=
# THERAPYPORTAL_PASSWORD=

# Only if the portal asks for a date of birth when you sign in: that date as
# MM/DD/YYYY. Tried once and never retried — the portal limits attempts.
# THERAPYPORTAL_DOB=

# server | fetchproxy. Default: server when email and password are both set,
# otherwise fetchproxy (relays through your signed-in portal tab; holds no
# credentials).
# THERAPYPORTAL_TRANSPORT=

# fetchproxy concentrator port. The whole fetchproxy fleet shares 37149 — the
# ContextMint Bridge extension dials that one port. Override only when hosting.
# THERAPYPORTAL_WS_PORT=37149

# Where downloaded files are written on the server transport (a path-delimiter
# list; ~ expands). Default ~/Downloads and ~/Documents. A per-call dest must
# resolve inside one. On the bridge transport the browser saves downloads to its
# own download folder.
# THERAPYPORTAL_OUTPUT_DIR=

# true returns downloaded bytes inline (base64) instead of writing to disk —
# for a hosted runner whose disk you cannot reach. Default false (disk).
# THERAPYPORTAL_INLINE_DOWNLOADS=

# Folders an upload's file_path must be inside (a path-delimiter list; ~
# expands). Default ~/Downloads, ~/Documents and ~/Desktop; $MCP_DATA_DIR/uploads
# when hosted.
# THERAPYPORTAL_UPLOAD_DIR=

# Confirm-gate behaviour for every write (from @chrischall/mcp-utils).
# MCP_CONFIRM_MODE: ask-user (default) returns a preview + confirmToken and
# requires a second call with that token; auto lets a capable host confirm in one
# step; an unrecognised value fails closed (refuse). MCP_CONFIRM_ELICITATION: on
# (default) lets the host confirm interactively; off forces the token round-trip.
# MCP_CONFIRM_MODE=
# MCP_CONFIRM_ELICITATION=
